  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "DumpModeDecode",
    "file": "gdal/gdal/frmts/gtiff/libtiff/tif_dumpmode.c",
    "description": "The root cause is an out-of-bounds/wild read in DumpModeDecode(): it copies `cc` bytes from `tif->tif_rawcp` with `_TIFFmemcpy()` after only checking `tif->tif_rawcc < cc`. There is no validation that `tif->tif_rawcp` actually points to a valid mapped/allocated raw buffer region of at least `cc` bytes. With malformed TIFF metadata/state, `tif_rawcp` can become attacker-controlled/invalid while `tif_rawcc` remains large enough, leading to memcpy from an invalid address and ASan SEGV. Crash manifests at `_TIFFmemcpy` called from DumpModeDecode during `TIFFReadEncodedTile`.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires a crafted GTiff input that drives the uncompressed dump-mode decode path (`tif->tif_decodetile == DumpModeDecode`) and corrupts/inconsistently sets raw tile/strip state so that `tif_rawcp` is invalid (or not backed by readable memory) but `tif_rawcc >= requested size`. Through GDAL flow (`GTiffDataset::ReadStrile` -> `TIFFReadEncodedTile` -> `TIFFFillTile`/decode), reading a tile causes DumpModeDecode to memcpy from that invalid raw pointer, causing the wild read crash."
  },
